{"id":"leg_press_calf_raise","name":"Leg-press calf raise","cue":"Knees straight; sink the heels, then rise onto your toes.","research":"Calf raise on the 45 degree leg press (science audit table B: a straight-knee calf raise like the standing one, the gastrocnemius works on straight legs). The leg press unit of leg_press.json is reused as it is (seat unit, back pad 15 deg above horizontal, rails, sled with its plate horns, the same pad fit table): hips pinned to the seat, hands on the side handles. Legs straight (knee 3, hip 66 so the foot lies flat on the plate at the neutral ankle: closed chain hip - knee + ankle = 60), toes out as the leg press stance (hip abduction 11, rotation 16). The plate is moved up its own plane so its lower edge sits 0.03 H under the toe-joint line: the balls of the feet rest on the lower edge and the heels hang free. Range of the standing calf raise (calf_raise.json): ankle 25 deg dorsiflexion (deep stretch, the sole 33 deg off the plate) to 10 deg of plantar flexion, tempo lift 1.0 / top 0.2 / lower 2.0 / stretch 1.5 s. The legs do not move: the foot turns about the ankle, the toes stay flat on the plate (toe ext follows the foot) and the sled follows the balls (sled 0.60 -> 0.93, solved per key so the toe-joint line touches the plate surface at every phase: skin gap 0.0002 H). Muscles: gastrocnemius (both heads, as the standing raise).","targets":{"tol":10,"note":"Calf raise on the leg press: straight knees, hip 66 so the foot is flat on the plate at -3 deg of ankle; the range is the standing raise (25 deg dorsiflexion to 10 deg plantar flexion).","A":{"trunk_flexion":-75,"hip_flexion":66,"knee_flexion":3,"ankle_dorsiflexion":25},"B":{"trunk_flexion":-75,"hip_flexion":66,"knee_flexion":3,"ankle_dorsiflexion":-10}},"muscles":{"primary":["gastroc"],"secondary":[],"side":"both"},"camera":{"az":110,"el":0,"dAz":0,"dEl":3,"fill":0.56,"note":"The standing calf raise view (az 110, el 3: from behind the lifter, the calves in profile as the heels drop below the plate edge). The plate and sled stand above and in front of the feet, the seat unit and the floor skids as in the leg press, so the horizon arc shows between them."},"rhythm":false,"motion":{"tempo":[1,0.2,2,1.5],"root":[0,0.3,0],"base":{"pelvis":{"flex":-75},"lumbar":{"flex":0},"thorax":{"flex":0},"neck":{"flex":2},"head":{"flex":0},"clav_l":{"elev":0,"pro":0},"arm_l":{"plane":-57,"elev":45,"rot":-45},"fore_l":{"flex":100}},"keys":{"A":{"thigh_l":{"flex":66,"abd":11.1,"rot":16.12},"shank_l":{"flex":3},"foot_l":{"dorsi":25},"toe_l":{"ext":-28},"m":{"sled":0.59681}},"M1":{"thigh_l":{"flex":66,"abd":11.1,"rot":16.12},"shank_l":{"flex":3},"foot_l":{"dorsi":19.167},"toe_l":{"ext":-22.167},"m":{"sled":0.65207}},"M2":{"thigh_l":{"flex":66,"abd":11.1,"rot":16.12},"shank_l":{"flex":3},"foot_l":{"dorsi":13.333},"toe_l":{"ext":-16.333},"m":{"sled":0.70821}},"M3":{"thigh_l":{"flex":66,"abd":11.1,"rot":16.12},"shank_l":{"flex":3},"foot_l":{"dorsi":7.5},"toe_l":{"ext":-10.5},"m":{"sled":0.76391}},"M4":{"thigh_l":{"flex":66,"abd":11.1,"rot":16.12},"shank_l":{"flex":3},"foot_l":{"dorsi":1.667},"toe_l":{"ext":-4.667},"m":{"sled":0.81917}},"M5":{"thigh_l":{"flex":66,"abd":11.1,"rot":16.12},"shank_l":{"flex":3},"foot_l":{"dorsi":-4.167},"toe_l":{"ext":1.167},"m":{"sled":0.87356}},"B":{"thigh_l":{"flex":66,"abd":11.1,"rot":16.12},"shank_l":{"flex":3},"foot_l":{"dorsi":-10},"toe_l":{"ext":7},"m":{"sled":0.92619}}},"timeline":[{"phase":"con","from":"A","via":["M1","M2","M3","M4","M5"],"at":[0,0.16666666666666666,0.3333333333333333,0.5,0.6666666666666666,0.8333333333333334,1],"to":"B","dur":1},{"phase":"hold","at":"B","dur":0.2},{"phase":"ecc","from":"B","via":["M5","M4","M3","M2","M1"],"at":[0,0.16666666666666666,0.3333333333333333,0.5,0.6666666666666666,0.8333333333333334,1],"to":"A","dur":2,"ease":"ecc"},{"phase":"pause","at":"A","dur":1.5}]},"pins":[{"landmark":"ischia_c","to":"seat_top"}],"contacts":[{"landmark":"thorax_back","to":"back","tol":0.012},{"landmark":"